  "period_note": "Q2 here is DERIVED FROM A HALF-YEARLY FILING (not a standalone Q2 report -- Bangladeshi banks do not file one). Income-statement figures are H1-CUMULATIVE (Jan 1 - 06-30, i.e. the full first half), exactly as the filing itself presents them -- NOT a discrete Apr-Jun-only figure. Solo section. Genuine loss half-year (net loss -679,326,543), driven by a large specific loan-loss provision (3,418,000,000 within the 4,122,500,000 provision subtotal, part of the 4,144,862,202 total provision) -- consistent with the Q1-2013 loss already seen in the 2014 Q1 filing's own comparative column (Q1-2013 alone was a larger -1,517,767,388 loss; implied Q2-2013-alone profit of ~838m reconciles exactly against the discrete Apr-Jun'13 column independently reported in the 2014 H1 filing). All values reconcile exactly (BS identity: 220,223,020,410+19,255,908,531=239,478,928,941; PBT-tax=PAT; opincome-opexpense=opprofit; opprofit-provision=PBT, all exact). Income-statement items are H1-CUMULATIVE (Jan-Jun), a 4-column table in the source also shows Apr-Jun discrete figures, not used here.",
